#
# Case 12 (INVARIANT): a CTE referenced twice is materialised, and the
# materialisation must be accounted for.
#
[log_start.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_cte_materialized
[log_stop.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_cte_materialized
Case 12 passed
#
# Case 13 (ACCURACY): ORDER BY over a UNION ALL.  The union result is
# materialised into a tmp table and then sorted, and this plan empties
# the tmp table through TABLE::empty_result_table() before it is
# dropped.  Emptying it releases everything it held, so a figure taken
# only at drop time would report an almost empty table for a statement
# that materialised 4000 rows.
#
[log_start.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_union_order_memory
[log_stop.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_union_order_memory
Case 13 passed
#
# Case 14 (ACCURACY): the same shape forced on to disk.  This is the
# query shape from PS-10854, which reported a single InnoDB page while
# the session temporary tablespace grew by tens of megabytes: the plan
# truncates the B-tree back to an empty root before the table is
# dropped, although the tablespace keeps every extent the table made it
# allocate.
#
Warnings:
Warning	48040	Tmp_table_size is set below 1MiB. The TEMPTABLE engine requires at least 1MiB table size, and will use that value instead. Please increase the limit to silence this warning.
[log_start.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_union_order_disk
[log_stop.inc] percona_slow_query_log.tts_union_order_disk
Case 14 passed
